            <ArticleTitle>[Lipoprotein (a) in physiological states and kidney diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>595-604</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present paper is a concise summary of contemporary knowledge of lipoprotein(a). Increased lipoprotein(a) concentration is an independent risk factor for atherogenesis. The treatment of choice of increased lipoprotein(a) concentration is causal--for example treatment of the nephrotic syndrome or renal transplantation. If this is not amenable, careful monitoring and elimination of additional risk factors of atherogenesis are mandatory.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
